    ["hygiene","ˈhaɪdʒiːn","n.","卫生","No, not until you've got the sign-off from Food [Hygiene].","S1E3 · Shopping","不行，得等食品卫生部门签字批准才行。","ˈhaɪdʒiːn"],
    ["appeal","əˈpiːl","n.","上诉；申诉","Charlie retreated to his own office to start work on the [appeal].","S3E2 · Porking","Charlie 退回他自己的办公室，开始准备上诉。","əˈpiːl"],
    ["resident","ˈrezɪdənt","adj.","常驻的","As it happened, the [resident] cynic was soon eating his words.","S4E4 · Cottaging","结果，这位常驻的怀疑派很快就被打脸了。","ˈrezɪdənt"],
    ["controversial","ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl","adj.","有争议的","So another thing I thought, which is [controversial], is putting prices up.","S5E4 · Updating","所以我想的另一件事，也是有争议的，就是涨价。","ˌkɑːntrəˈvɜːrʃ(ə)l"],
    ["loophole","ˈluːphəʊl","n.","漏洞","This was the best [loophole] of them all.","S2E7 · Scheming","这是所有漏洞里最好的一个。","ˈluːphoʊl"],
    ["brewery","ˈbruːəri","n.","啤酒厂","The spring barley from here, if the quality's good enough, will go to the [brewery] and will be made into Hawkstone beer.","S2E6 · Counselling","这里的春大麦如果品质够好，会送去啤酒厂，酿成 Hawkstone 啤酒。","ˈbruːəri"],
    ["optimistic","ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk","adj.","乐观的","However, now we had the sleeper plan in place, I was much more [optimistic] that we would.","S3E6 · Mushrooming","不过，既然枕木计划已经就位，我对我们能做到乐观多了。","ˌɑːptɪˈmɪstɪk"],
    ["desperate","ˈdespərət","adj.","绝望的；不顾一切的","So, in these [desperate] times, I came up with a desperate measure.","S1E3 · Shopping","所以，在这种走投无路的时候，我想出了一个不顾一切的办法。","ˈdespərət"],
    ["temporary","ˈtemprəri","adj.","临时的","So we've got that out, we've got some clay to create a [temporary] dam while we build the proper dam.","S3E3 · Jobbing","我们把那个清出来了，用一些黏土先筑一道临时坝，同时修正式的坝。","ˈtempəreri"],
    ["underestimate","ˌʌndərˈestɪmeɪt","v.","低估","Do not [underestimate] them.","S3E6 · Mushrooming","不要低估它们。","ˌʌndərˈestɪmeɪt"],
    ["tremendous","trəˈmendəs","adj.","极好的；巨大的","But this was no time for pessimism, as the pond was now looking [tremendous] and that's not all.","S1E4 · Wilding","不过现在可不是悲观的时候，因为池塘看起来棒极了，而且还不止这些。","trəˈmendəs"],
    ["crucial","ˈkruːʃl","adj.","至关重要的","The [crucial] harvesting month was also refusing to play ball.","S3E8 · Calculating","关键的收割月也不肯配合。","ˈkruːʃ(ə)l"],
    ["negotiate","nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt","v.","谈判；协商","The price is dictated to you rather than you being able to [negotiate] or set a price.","S2E5 · Council-ing","价格是别人定给你的，你根本没法谈判或自己定价。","nɪˈɡoʊʃieɪt"],
    ["abattoir","ˈæbətwɑː(r)","n.","屠宰场","There are now only 49 local [abattoirs] left in the whole country.","S4E2 · Pubbing","现在全国只剩下49家本地屠宰场了。","ˈæbətwɑːr"],
    ["accommodate","əˈkɒmədeɪt","v.","容纳；适应","You know, our starting point is we hope we can [accommodate] the consequences of this.","S4E2 · Pubbing","你知道，我们的出发点是希望能承受这件事带来的后果。","əˈkɑːmədeɪt"],
    ["affordable","əˈfɔːdəbl","adj.","负担得起的","I'm going to make [affordable] food.","S4E1 · Solo-ing","我要做大家吃得起的食物。","əˈfɔːrdəb(ə)l"],
    ["aggressive","əˈɡresɪv","adj.","好斗的；有攻击性的","You're going to see the [aggressive] males first.","S3E3 · Jobbing","你会先看到那些好斗的公的。","əˈɡresɪv"],
    ["alarming","əˈlɑːmɪŋ","adj.","令人担忧的","And just as we were finishing that, Charlie arrived and made a rather [alarming] observation.","S4E8 · Landlording","就在我们快弄完的时候，Charlie 来了，还发现了一个相当令人担忧的情况。","əˈlɑːrmɪŋ"],
    ["anxiety","æŋˈzaɪəti","n.","焦虑","Have you got any [anxiety] about it?","S2E3 · Schmoozing","你对这事有什么焦虑吗？","æŋˈzaɪəti"],
    ["apprentice","əˈprentɪs","n.","学徒","My young [apprentice] is doing well.","S3E4 · Harrowing","我的年轻学徒干得不错。","əˈprentɪs"],
    ["approval","əˈpruːvl","n.","批准；认可","But before he could start work, I had to get [approval] from the local authority.","S2E3 · Schmoozing","但在他开工之前，我得先拿到地方政府的批准。","əˈpruːv(ə)l"],
    ["assessment","əˈsesmənt","n.","评估","No, but we might need a risk [assessment].","S1E3 · Shopping","不用，不过我们可能需要做个风险评估。","əˈsesmənt"],
    ["astonishing","əˈstɒnɪʃɪŋ","adj.","惊人的","But all of us knew that to try and stop this [astonishing] attack on British farming, fun wouldn't cut it.","S5E1 · Operating","但我们都知道，要阻止这场对英国农业惊人的打击，光靠热闹是不够的。","əˈstɑːnɪʃɪŋ"],
    ["atmosphere","ˈætməsfɪə(r)","n.","大气；氛围","Is it just moisture in the [atmosphere]?","S1E8 · Harvesting","只是空气中的湿气吗？","ˈætməsfɪr"],
    ["auction","ˈɔːkʃn","n.","拍卖","So I decided to go to my first-ever cattle [auction] and buy some cows.","S4E6 · Splurging","所以我决定去参加我人生第一场牛拍卖会，买几头牛。","ˈɔːkʃn"],
    ["authority","ɔːˈθɒrəti","n.","当局；权威","Because Lisa's definition of local produce had come to the attention of the [authorities].","S1E7 · Fluffing","因为 Lisa 对“本地农产品”的定义已经引起了当局的注意。","əˈθɔːrəti"],
    ["autonomous","ɔːˈtɒnəməs","adj.","自主的；自动驾驶的","This is where [autonomous] driving really makes sense.","S5E4 · Updating","这就是自动驾驶真正有意义的地方。","ɔːˈtɑːnəməs"],
    ["bacteria","bækˈtɪəriə","n.","细菌","Type of [bacteria] found in the gut of animals and humans.","S1E3 · Shopping","一种存在于动物和人类肠道里的细菌。","bækˈtɪriə"],
    ["bankrupt","ˈbæŋkrʌpt","adj.","破产的","Literally a butterfly can flap its wings in China and you go [bankrupt].","S3E8 · Calculating","真的是，一只蝴蝶在中国扇扇翅膀，你就可能破产。","ˈbæŋkrʌpt"],
    ["barrier","ˈbæriə(r)","n.","关口；障碍","And found that Kaleb's outgoings had now gone through the £100,000 [barrier].","S3E6 · Mushrooming","然后发现 Kaleb 的开支已经突破了10万英镑的关口。","ˈbæriər"],
    ["bizarre","bɪˈzɑː(r)","adj.","古怪的","Well, I know it sounds a little [bizarre].","S1E7 · Fluffing","嗯，我知道这听起来有点怪。","bɪˈzɑːr"],
    ["bureaucratic","ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk","adj.","官僚的","Inside, Charlie's [bureaucratic] bombs kept on falling.","S1E3 · Shopping","屋里，Charlie 的官僚炸弹还在接连落下。","ˌbjʊrəˈkrætɪk"],
    ["cautious","ˈkɔːʃəs","adj.","谨慎的","I'd be highly [cautious] about doing anything around these banks.","S3E2 · Porking","在这些河岸附近做任何事，我都会非常谨慎。","ˈkɔːʃəs"],
    ["certificate","səˈtɪfɪkət","n.","证书","Then, there was the annual inspection needed to renew my Red Tractor [certificate].","S2E8 · Climaxing","接着还有一年一度的检查，要靠它来续我的“红拖拉机”认证证书。","sərˈtɪfɪkət"],
    ["climate","ˈklaɪmət","n.","气候","The [climate]'s changing and we have a truly idiotic government.","S5E3 · Tripping","气候在变，而我们有一个真正愚蠢的政府。","ˈklaɪmət"],
    ["collapse","kəˈlæps","v.","倒塌","Anybody puts any weight on there, that'll just [collapse].","S3E5 · Healing","谁要是往那上面压点重量，它就会塌。","kəˈlæps"],
    ["colleague","ˈkɒliːɡ","n.","同事","And then there's some doors over there from a house that my [colleagues] blew up.","S1E6 · Melting","那边还有几扇门，是从我同事炸掉的一栋房子上拆来的。","ˈkɑːliːɡ"],
    ["commercial","kəˈmɜːʃl","adj.","商业的","And the issue is you've got a [commercial] need for mustard, which is one of the biggest sellers in the shop.","S5E7 · Sickening","问题是，芥末有商业需求，它是店里最畅销的商品之一。","kəˈmɜːrʃ(ə)l"],
    ["compatible","kəmˈpætəbl","adj.","兼容的","'Cause the sprayer isn't [compatible] with it.","S4E2 · Pubbing","因为喷雾器跟它不兼容。","kəmˈpætəb(ə)l"],
    ["competition","ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃn","n.","竞争对手；竞争","You've brought it in a bag from our closest [competition].","S1E7 · Fluffing","你装它的袋子是从我们最近的竞争对手那儿拿来的。","ˌkɑːmpəˈtɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["complaint","kəmˈpleɪnt","n.","投诉；抱怨","Despite my attempts to win over the locals, I was still receiving a steady stream of [complaints].","S2E3 · Schmoozing","尽管我努力讨好当地人，投诉还是源源不断地来。","kəmˈpleɪnt"],
    ["concept","ˈkɒnsept","n.","概念；理念","The [concept] of serving the nose to tail of your cows in this pub does not work.","S4E6 · Splurging","在这家酒吧里把牛从头到尾都做成菜的这个理念行不通。","ˈkɑːnsept"],
    ["conflicted","kənˈflɪktɪd","adj.","矛盾的；纠结的","So, I went down to the pond with a net, feeling weirdly [conflicted].","S1E7 · Fluffing","于是我拿着网去了池塘，心里莫名地纠结。","kənˈflɪktɪd"],
    ["congestion","kənˈdʒestʃən","n.","拥堵","So, you're gonna need to pay that [congestion] charge.","S1E7 · Fluffing","所以你得交那笔拥堵费。","kənˈdʒestʃən"],
    ["consequence","ˈkɒnsɪkwəns","n.","后果","I mean, this is the kind of little tiny [consequence] of the quarantine that you don't think about.","S1E5 · Pan (dem) icking","我是说，这就是隔离带来的那种你想不到的小小后果。","ˈkɑːnsɪkwens"],
    ["consistent","kənˈsɪstənt","adj.","一致的；相符的","Would not be compatible or [consistent] in scale \"with the existing farming business\"","S2E6 · Counselling","在规模上与“现有农场业务”既不相称也不一致。","kənˈsɪstənt"],
    ["contingency","kənˈtɪndʒənsi","n.","应急费用；意外情况","450,000 with a 50,000 [contingency].","S4E2 · Pubbing","45万，外加5万的应急预算。","kənˈtɪndʒənsi"],
    ["operational","ˌɒpəˈreɪʃənl","adj.","可运营的","You reckon you could get this [operational] for 450,000 - with a £50,000 contingency?","S4E2 · Pubbing","你觉得45万就能让它投入运营，再留5万英镑应急？","ˌɑːpəˈreɪʃən(ə)l"],
    ["contractor","kənˈtræktə(r)","n.","承包商","Because why would you ever employ a fencing [contractor] when you have the Solo Track?","S2E1 · Surviving","既然有了 Solo Track，你干嘛还要雇围栏承包商？","ˈkɑːntræktər"],
    ["contribution","ˌkɒntrɪˈbjuːʃn","n.","贡献","But even though I'd sampled many glasses of this delicious new lager, I felt I should make a [contribution].","S2E4 · Badgering","不过，尽管我已经品尝了好多杯这款美味的新啤酒，我觉得自己也该出点力。","ˌkɑːntrɪˈbjuːʃ(ə)n"],
    ["immense","ɪˈmens","adj.","巨大的","Your contribution is [immense], I've gotta be honest with you.","S4E6 · Splurging","你的贡献非常大，我得跟你说实话。","ɪˈmens"],
    ["cooperative","kəʊˈɒpərətɪv","n.","合作社","The meeting ended with an agreement to form a sort of [cooperative].","S2E5 · Council-ing","会议最后达成一致，成立一个类似合作社的组织。","koʊˈɑːpərətɪv"],
    ["criteria","kraɪˈtɪəriə","n.","标准（复数）","And they've put a list down here of things that don't meet that [criteria].","S2E5 · Council-ing","他们在这里列了一份清单，写的是不符合那些标准的事项。","kraɪˈtɪriə"],
    ["deadline","ˈdedlaɪn","n.","截止期限","As a result of everything, there was now no hope of hitting Charlie's [deadlines].","S1E1 · Tractoring","这么一折腾，Charlie 定的截止期限已经完全没希望赶上了。","ˈdedlaɪn"],
    ["decline","dɪˈklaɪn","n.","衰落；减少","The first pub we visited was a heartfelt reminder of this sad [decline].","S4E3 · Crawling","我们去的第一家酒吧，令人痛心地提醒了我们这种衰落。","dɪˈklaɪn"],
    ["dehydration","ˌdiːhaɪˈdreɪʃn","n.","脱水","We're warming up his body and this is trying to correct his [dehydration] really.","S3E3 · Jobbing","我们在给它暖身子，这其实是在纠正它的脱水。","ˌdiːhaɪˈdreɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["deliberately","dɪˈlɪbərətli","adv.","故意地","I [deliberately] haven't given them names.","S1E2 · Sheeping","我故意没给它们起名字。","dɪˈlɪbərətli"],
    ["delicate","ˈdelɪkət","adj.","精细的；需小心处理的","Once I'd minced all the stumps, I moved on to another wood-based job, only this one was much more [delicate].","S4E7 · Hurrying","把树桩全都粉碎之后，我转去干另一件跟木头有关的活儿，只不过这次要精细得多。","ˈdelɪkət"],
    ["deprive","dɪˈpraɪv","v.","剥夺","If you plough, you turn the soil over so that the weeds are [deprived] of light and oxygen and then they die.","S4E3 · Crawling","犁地就是把土翻过来，让杂草得不到阳光和氧气，然后就死了。","dɪˈpraɪv"],
    ["detect","dɪˈtekt","v.","检测；发现","We can actually [detect] those spots and actually only kill those weeds without touching the rest.","S5E3 · Tripping","我们其实能识别出那些点位，只除掉那些杂草，别的都不碰。","dɪˈtekt"],
    ["diagnose","ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz","v.","诊断","I went back to the farm office and tried to [diagnose] the problem myself.","S1E2 · Sheeping","我回到农场办公室，试着自己诊断问题出在哪。","ˌdaɪəɡˈnoʊs"],
    ["dilemma","dɪˈlemə","n.","两难境地","So can you see my [dilemma]?","S5E7 · Sickening","所以你明白我的两难了吗？","dɪˈlemə"],
    ["disappointment","ˌdɪsəˈpɔɪntmənt","n.","失望；令人失望的事","And we've had the usual year of rows, difficulties, bad weather, [disappointments], deaths.","S3E8 · Calculating","我们照常过了一年：吵架、困难、坏天气、失望、死亡。","ˌdɪsəˈpɔɪntmənt"],
    ["discrepancy","dɪˈskrepənsi","n.","差异；不符","The control unit detects a [discrepancy] between the oil pressure reading and the operating status of the transmission.","S4E2 · Pubbing","控制单元检测到油压读数与变速箱运行状态之间存在差异。","dɪˈskrepənsi"],
    ["disease","dɪˈziːz","n.","疾病","He just wanted to vaccinate the sheep against a rather nasty new [disease].","S5E2 · Storming","他只是想给羊接种疫苗，预防一种相当难缠的新病。","dɪˈziːz"],
    ["vaccinate","ˈvæksɪneɪt","v.","接种疫苗","And I don't believe that science cannot work out how to [vaccinate] cows.","S5E8 · Reaping","我不相信科学没法解决给牛接种疫苗的问题。","ˈvæksɪneɪt"],
    ["disobedient","ˌdɪsəˈbiːdiənt","adj.","不听话的","My cows are as [disobedient] as my sheep, it's pouring with rain, my shoes are covered in excrement.","S2E2 · Cowering","我的牛跟我的羊一样不听话，大雨倾盆，我的鞋上全是粪。","ˌdɪsəˈbiːdiənt"],
    ["disruption","dɪsˈrʌpʃn","n.","中断；扰乱","Risk of flooding, risk of transport [disruption].","S1E1 · Tractoring","有洪水风险，有交通中断的风险。","dɪsˈrʌpʃn"],
    ["distribute","dɪˈstrɪbjuːt","v.","分配；分布","The brush will then [distribute] that paint onto the tyre, which will leave a mark that I can follow in the field.","S4E1 · Solo-ing","刷子会把油漆涂到轮胎上，留下一道标记，我在地里就能沿着它走。","dɪˈstrɪbjuːt"],
    ["dormant","ˈdɔːmənt","adj.","休眠的","That will deprive the potato of its ability to grow, and it will just lay [dormant] in the soil.","S1E3 · Shopping","那样会让土豆失去生长能力，它就只会在土里休眠。","ˈdɔːrmənt"],
    ["drawback","ˈdrɔːbæk","n.","缺点","There was one [drawback] with the AgBot, though: it's not allowed on the public highway.","S5E5 · Decapitating","不过 AgBot 有一个缺点：它不允许上公路。","ˈdrɔːbæk"],
    ["dwindling","ˈdwɪndlɪŋ","adj.","日益减少的","It would help the soil, it would help local farmers and local businesses, and it would help us offset the [dwindling] government subsidies.","S2E5 · Council-ing","这对土壤有好处，对本地农民和本地商家有好处，也能帮我们弥补日益减少的政府补贴。","ˈdwɪndlɪŋ"],
    ["ecologically","ˌiːkəˈlɒdʒɪkli","adv.","生态地；环保地","I thought they'd be a cheap and easy way of keeping the grass down [ecologically].","S1E6 · Melting","我以为它们会是一种又便宜又省事、还环保的除草方式。","ˌiːkəˈlɑːdʒɪkli"],
    ["emergency","ɪˈmɜːdʒənsi","n.","紧急情况","Sadly though, there was no time to celebrate because the next [emergency] beckoned.","S1E6 · Melting","可惜没时间庆祝，因为下一个紧急情况又来了。","ɪˈmɜːrdʒənsi"],
    ["endangered","ɪnˈdeɪndʒəd","adj.","濒危的","And how many of them are [endangered]?","S5E7 · Sickening","它们当中有多少是濒危的？","ɪnˈdeɪndʒərd"],
    ["enforcement","ɪnˈfɔːsmənt","n.","执行；强制","The council served us with an [enforcement] notice, telling us it had to close.","S3E1 · Unfarming","议会给我们发了一份执行通知，告诉我们必须关门。","ɪnˈfɔːrsmənt"],
    ["enormous","ɪˈnɔːməs","adj.","巨大的","But, with the [enormous] plough actually in the soil, I was going nowhere.","S4E3 · Crawling","可是那台巨大的犁真插进土里之后，我就寸步难行了。","ɪˈnɔːrməs"],
    ["equivalent","ɪˈkwɪvələnt","n.","等量；相等物","So, it's reckoned ten thousand litres of water over a hectare gives you the [equivalent] of one millimetre of rain.","S5E7 · Sickening","据估算，一公顷地上浇一万升水，相当于一毫米的降雨。","ɪˈkwɪvələnt"],
    ["erratic","ɪˈrætɪk","adj.","反复无常的","There were signs that the [erratic] weather had ruined this crop as well.","S3E8 · Calculating","有迹象表明，反复无常的天气把这茬庄稼也毁了。","ɪˈrætɪk"],
    ["essential","ɪˈsenʃl","adj.","必要的","Now is the time for everyone to stop non-[essential] contact with others.","S1E4 · Wilding","现在是所有人停止非必要接触的时候了。","ɪˈsenʃ(ə)l"],
    ["evaporate","ɪˈvæpəreɪt","v.","蒸发","You know, I mean it's [evaporated] already and blown away.","S1E6 · Melting","你看，它已经蒸发掉、被风吹走了。","ɪˈvæpəreɪt"],
    ["evidence","ˈevɪdəns","n.","证据","So you've got some previous kind of [evidence] here of having some crayfish.","S3E3 · Jobbing","所以这里你有一些以前有过小龙虾的证据。","ˈevɪdəns"],
    ["extraordinary","ɪkˈstrɔːdnri","adj.","非凡的","What's more, the [extraordinary] lion's mane mushrooms had started to appear.","S3E6 · Mushrooming","更妙的是，那些奇特的猴头菇已经开始冒出来了。","ɪkˈstrɔːrdəneri"],
    ["fluctuation","ˌflʌktʃuˈeɪʃn","n.","波动","Because of the [fluctuations] we saw in the price of wheat","S3E8 · Calculating","因为我们看到小麦价格的波动","ˌflʌktʃuˈeɪʃn"],
    ["foundation","faʊnˈdeɪʃn","n.","地基","And when it finally eased up, this is what the shop's [foundations] looked like.","S1E3 · Shopping","等雨终于小了，商店的地基成了这个样子。","faʊnˈdeɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["frantic","ˈfræntɪk","adj.","忙乱的","After a [frantic] day, it was time to shut the doors","S1E3 · Shopping","忙乱了一整天，到了关门的时候","ˈfræntɪk"],
    ["genuine","ˈdʒenjuɪn","adj.","真诚的","You have to listen to people, you have to be [genuine], you have to show that you care.","S2E3 · Schmoozing","你得倾听别人，你得真诚，你得表现出你在乎。","ˈdʒenjuɪn"],
    ["hardship","ˈhɑːdʃɪp","n.","困苦","And they're facing unprecedented [hardship] now.","S2E5 · Council-ing","而他们现在正面临前所未有的困境。","ˈhɑːrdʃɪp"],
    ["hazardous","ˈhæzədəs","adj.","危险的","Even though my tractor was extremely nimble and just the right size, the cross country route to the water tank was extremely [hazardous].","S1E2 · Sheeping","尽管我的拖拉机非常灵活、大小正合适，但越野去水箱的那条路极其危险。","ˈhæzərdəs"],
    ["heatwave","ˈhiːtweɪv","n.","热浪","Sadly, though, the recent [heatwave] had taken its toll.","S1E7 · Fluffing","可惜，最近的热浪造成了损失。","ˈhiːtweɪv"],
    ["hectare","ˈhekteə(r)","n.","公顷","At the moment it's saying a quarter of a tonne to the [hectare].","S3E8 · Calculating","目前显示的是每公顷四分之一吨。","ˈhekter"],
    ["hindsight","ˈhaɪndsaɪt","n.","事后看来","Well, I got them all in, which was, I think with [hindsight], a mistake.","S4E2 · Pubbing","嗯，我把它们全都弄进来了，事后看来，我觉得这是个错误。","ˈhaɪndsaɪt"],
    ["identical","aɪˈdentɪkl","adj.","完全相同的","I had a pair [identical] to that.","S1E4 · Wilding","我以前有一副跟那个一模一样的。","aɪˈdentɪk(ə)l"],
    ["imminent","ˈɪmɪnənt","adj.","即将发生的","So, full scale egg production was [imminent].","S1E3 · Shopping","所以，全面的鸡蛋生产就要开始了。","ˈɪmɪnənt"],
    ["impact","ˈɪmpækt","n.","影响","Apparently eating half a cow is the same environmental [impact] as one person flying to Australia.","S2E5 · Council-ing","据说吃半头牛对环境的影响，跟一个人坐飞机去澳大利亚一样。","ˈɪmpækt"],
    ["implement","ˈɪmplɪmənt","n.","农具；工具","You then need some [implements] to go on the back of it.","S1E1 · Tractoring","然后你还需要一些农具挂在它后面。","ˈɪmplɪmənt"],
    ["inaccessible","ˌɪnækˈsesəbl","adj.","难以到达的","Which was to clear the brambles in all the [inaccessible] parts of the farm.","S4E6 · Splurging","也就是清理农场所有难以到达的地方的荆棘。","ˌɪnəkˈsesəb(ə)l"],
    ["indefinitely","ɪnˈdefɪnətli","adv.","无限期地","Plus, you're also building health into your soil so you can farm [indefinitely].","S3E2 · Porking","另外，你也在为土壤积累健康，这样你就可以无限期地种下去。","ɪnˈdefɪnətli"],
    ["indisputable","ˌɪndɪˈspjuːtəbl","adj.","无可争辩的","The runway turned out to be [indisputable] evidence that the self-proclaimed \"best farmer at Diddly Squat\" had screwed up.","S2E4 · Badgering","那条跑道成了无可争辩的证据，证明那位自封的“Diddly Squat 最佳农民”搞砸了。","ˌɪndɪˈspjuːtəb(ə)l"],
    ["infection","ɪnˈfekʃn","n.","感染","Ulcerated area appears at the top of the hoof, [infection] spreads under the horn and down to the toe.","S1E2 · Sheeping","蹄子顶部出现溃烂，感染扩散到蹄角下面，一直到脚趾。","ɪnˈfekʃ(ə)n"],
    ["infrastructure","ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃə(r)","n.","基础设施","So give us the [infrastructure] to make it something brilliant.","S3E4 · Harrowing","所以给我们基础设施，让它变得出色。","ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃər"],
    ["ingenious","ɪnˈdʒiːniəs","adj.","巧妙的","Today, I was doing important work, because I've come up with an [ingenious] plan.","S1E5 · Pan (dem) icking","今天我在做重要的事，因为我想出了一个巧妙的计划。","ɪnˈdʒiːniəs"],
    ["initiative","ɪˈnɪʃətɪv","n.","倡议；计划","They'd been invited to Downing Street to talk to the Prime Minister about his \"Back British Farm to Fork\" [initiative].","S3E6 · Mushrooming","他们受邀去唐宁街，跟首相谈他的“从英国农场到餐桌”倡议。","ɪˈnɪʃətɪv"],
    ["instinct","ˈɪnstɪŋkt","n.","直觉；本能","Convinced my [instincts] were right, I'd already put an offer in.","S4E2 · Pubbing","我确信自己的直觉没错，已经出价了。","ˈɪnstɪŋkt"],
    ["interfere","ˌɪntəˈfɪə(r)","v.","干扰；乱动","Please do not [interfere] with this alarm or any of its sensors.","S4E2 · Pubbing","请勿乱动本警报器或其任何传感器。","ˌɪntərˈfɪr"],
    ["invasive","ɪnˈveɪsɪv","adj.","入侵的","In case I squash an [invasive] crayfish?","S3E3 · Jobbing","万一我踩扁一只入侵的小龙虾呢？","ɪnˈveɪsɪv"],
    ["irrigation","ˌɪrɪˈɡeɪʃn","n.","灌溉","So this is an [irrigation] and an aeration tube.","S1E6 · Melting","所以这是一根灌溉兼通气的管子。","ˌɪrɪˈɡeɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["isolation","ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn","n.","隔离","Back at the yard, we made a pneumonia [isolation] pen for the little calf and her mum.","S5E8 · Reaping","回到院子里，我们给小牛犊和它妈妈搭了一个肺炎隔离栏。","ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn"],
    ["maintenance","ˈmeɪntənəns","n.","维护；照料","However, while building the new pig houses, I was reminded that the woods were in urgent need of some [maintenance].","S3E3 · Jobbing","不过，在建新猪舍的时候，我想起林子也急需打理了。","ˈmeɪntənəns"],
    ["microorganism","ˌmaɪkrəʊˈɔːɡənɪzəm","n.","微生物","It could be that there's some [microorganism] in there that's eating the sugar.","S3E7 · Parking","可能里面有某种微生物在吃糖。","ˌmaɪkroʊˈɔːrɡənɪzəm"],
    ["migration","maɪˈɡreɪʃn","n.","迁徙","Bramble, fantastic for the warblers to put on fat for their [migration] to Africa.","S1E4 · Wilding","荆棘对莺来说很棒，能让它们在迁徙去非洲之前长膘。","maɪˈɡreɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["milestone","ˈmaɪlstəʊn","n.","里程碑","And today was yet another [milestone] in their adolescence, because two of them were due to be dehorned.","S2E6 · Counselling","今天是它们青春期的又一个里程碑，因为其中两头要去角了。","ˈmaɪlstoʊn"],
    ["monoculture","ˈmɒnəʊkʌltʃə(r)","n.","单一种植","So what we've got to get away from is [monocultures].","S3E2 · Porking","所以我们必须摆脱的是单一种植。","ˈmɑːnəkʌltʃər"],
    ["nuisance","ˈnjuːsns","n.","麻烦；讨厌的事","The issues and delays were a constant [nuisance].","S2E8 · Climaxing","这些问题和拖延一直很烦人。","ˈnuːs(ə)ns"],
    ["obstacle","ˈɒbstəkl","n.","障碍物","If you see an [obstacle], and you do that, you're going to hit it.","S3E4 · Harrowing","要是你看到障碍物，还那样做，你就会撞上去。","ˈɑːbstək(ə)l"],
    ["opposition","ˌɒpəˈzɪʃn","n.","反对","That we'd opened a restaurant in the face of such a relentless barrage of [opposition].","S2E8 · Climaxing","我们顶着如此持续不断的反对，把餐厅开起来了。","ˌɑːpəˈzɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["organic","ɔːˈɡænɪk","adj.","有机的","In [organic], the main thing is about not using any chemicals.","S3E2 · Porking","有机种植最主要的就是不用任何化学品。","ɔːrˈɡænɪk"],
    ["outbreak","ˈaʊtbreɪk","n.","（疾病）爆发","And that was the start of an [outbreak].","S2E5 · Council-ing","那就是一场疫情爆发的开始。","ˈaʊtbreɪk"],
    ["overwhelmed","ˌəʊvəˈwelmd","adj.","不知所措的","We were [overwhelmed] by what happened when the show first aired, traffic and mud and chaos and speeding.","S2E3 · Schmoozing","节目第一次播出后发生的事让我们不知所措：交通堵塞、泥泞、混乱和超速。","ˌoʊvərˈwelmd"],
    ["pandemic","pænˈdemɪk","n.","大流行病","I mean, there's a [pandemic] going on.","S1E7 · Fluffing","我是说，现在可是疫情大流行。","pænˈdemɪk"],
    ["paramount","ˈpærəmaʊnt","adj.","至关重要的","I've told you again and again you've got three qualities in the wheat which are [paramount] to make it milling, and particularly for pasta.","S4E8 · Landlording","我一遍遍跟你说过，小麦有三项品质对做面粉、尤其是做意面至关重要。","ˈpærəmaʊnt"],
    ["parched","pɑːtʃt","adj.","干透的","After the driest summer for 87 years, the ground is [parched] and as hard as concrete.","S3E1 · Unfarming","经历了87年来最干旱的夏天，地面干透了，硬得像混凝土。","pɑːrtʃt"],
    ["pasture","ˈpɑːstʃə(r)","n.","牧场","Then it was time to move the EasyCare sheep and their lambs to a new [pasture].","S5E7 · Sickening","接着该把 EasyCare 羊和它们的小羊转到一片新牧场了。","ˈpæstʃər"],
    ["perimeter","pəˈrɪmɪtə(r)","n.","周界；边界","And then, draw up the lines of their invisible [perimeter] fence.","S4E5 · Endgaming","然后画出它们那道看不见的周界围栏的线。","pəˈrɪmɪtər"],
    ["pessimistic","ˌpesɪˈmɪstɪk","adj.","悲观的","You know my sort of [pessimistic] budget on how much this was all gonna cost?","S4E7 · Hurrying","你知道我对这一切要花多少钱做的那个比较悲观的预算吧？","ˌpesɪˈmɪstɪk"],
    ["phenomenal","fəˈnɒmɪnl","adj.","非凡的；惊人的","I'm an incredible athlete, and can run at [phenomenal] speeds, but I can't keep up with the sheep.","S1E2 · Sheeping","我是个了不起的运动员，跑起来速度惊人，可我还是追不上羊。","fəˈnɑːmɪn(ə)l"],
    ["plentiful","ˈplentɪfl","adj.","大量的","In the fields, rats as [plentiful] as hares ravaged the cabbages.","S4E3 · Crawling","地里的老鼠跟野兔一样多，把卷心菜糟蹋得不成样子。","ˈplentɪf(ə)l"],
    ["pollution","pəˈluːʃn","n.","污染","So we've gotta let them know where we're planting each hedge and each bush so there's not light [pollution] coming across the valley.","S2E3 · Schmoozing","所以我们得让他们知道每道树篱、每丛灌木种在哪里，免得有光污染照到山谷对面。","pəˈluːʃ(ə)n"],
    ["precarious","prɪˈkeəriəs","adj.","不稳的；危险的","The one that's most [precarious] is here.","S5E2 · Storming","最不稳的是这儿这个。","prɪˈkeriəs"],
    ["precaution","prɪˈkɔːʃn","n.","预防措施","What [precautions] have you taken to stop a flood risk?","S3E3 · Jobbing","你们采取了什么预防措施来防止洪水风险？","prɪˈkɔːʃn"],
    ["predator","ˈpredətə(r)","n.","捕食者","In the wild, there's [predators] out there, she'll clean up after her, so therefore the predators can't smell the baby.","S2E5 · Council-ing","在野外有捕食者，它会把身后清理干净，这样捕食者就闻不到幼崽的气味。","ˈpredətər"],
    ["prestigious","preˈstɪdʒəs","adj.","有声望的","And he'd come to see me because Diddly Squat had been invited to host a [prestigious] competition.","S2E6 · Counselling","他来找我，是因为 Diddly Squat 受邀主办一场很有声望的比赛。","preˈstiːdʒəs"],
    ["prosecute","ˈprɒsɪkjuːt","v.","起诉","Then you'd be [prosecuted] and you could potentially have a prison term.","S1E4 · Wilding","那样你就会被起诉，还可能坐牢。","ˈprɑːsɪkjuːt"],
    ["prospect","ˈprɒspekt","n.","前景；可能性","Clearly, though, the hens weren't thrilled at the [prospect] of living in LEGOLAND.","S1E3 · Shopping","不过很明显，母鸡们对住进乐高乐园这个前景并不兴奋。","ˈprɑːspekt"],
    ["quandary","ˈkwɒndəri","n.","进退两难","I was now in a [quandary].","S1E8 · Harvesting","我现在进退两难了。","ˈkwɑːndəri"],
    ["recovery","rɪˈkʌvəri","n.","康复","Well, I just wish you a very, very speedy [recovery].","S5E7 · Sickening","好吧，我只祝你早日康复。","rɪˈkʌvəri"],
    ["redundant","rɪˈdʌndənt","adj.","被裁员的；多余的","I was made [redundant] from the grind of day-to-day farming duties.","S4E1 · Solo-ing","我被从日复一日的繁重农活里“裁”了下来。","rɪˈdʌndənt"],
    ["regenerative","rɪˈdʒenərətɪv","adj.","再生的","[Regenerative] farming is a way of farming which tries to copy natural systems.","S3E2 · Porking","再生农业是一种试图模仿自然系统的耕作方式。","rɪˈdʒenərətɪv"],
    ["renovation","ˌrenəˈveɪʃn","n.","翻新","With the pub [renovation] underway, I got back to the business of providing it with food.","S4E6 · Splurging","酒吧翻新正在进行，我又回去忙着给它供应食材。","ˌrenəˈveɪʃ(ə)n"],
    ["reservoir","ˈrezəvwɑː(r)","n.","储液罐；水库","No one knows where the brake [reservoir] is on this thing.","S4E2 · Pubbing","没人知道这东西的刹车油壶在哪儿。","ˈrezərvwɑːr"],
    ["resistant","rɪˈzɪstənt","adj.","有抵抗力的","Then it'll have time to strengthen like that and then it'll be [resistant], and it'll be harder to get anything out of it.","S4E6 · Splurging","然后它就有时间那样变强，变得有抵抗力，就更难从里面弄出东西来了。","rɪˈzɪstənt"],
    ["ruthless","ˈruːθləs","adj.","无情的","The whole driving of that was just [ruthless].","S1E6 · Melting","那一路开得简直毫不留情。","ˈruːθləs"],
    ["shortage","ˈʃɔːtɪdʒ","n.","短缺","The water [shortage] was a serious problem, but it wasn't the only thing that was bothering me.","S1E6 · Melting","缺水是个严重的问题，但这不是唯一让我烦心的事。","ˈʃɔːrtɪdʒ"],
    ["sophisticated","səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd","adj.","老练的；精致的","Once Lucca had finished cooking, I just needed someone with a [sophisticated] palate to taste it.","S3E5 · Healing","等 Lucca 做完菜，我只需要找个口味讲究的人来尝一尝。","səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd"],
    ["spectacular","spekˈtækjələ(r)","adj.","壮观的；惊人的","And when the machine finally fell silent for the night, the results were [spectacular].","S1E4 · Wilding","当机器终于在夜里停下来时，效果非常壮观。","spekˈtækjələr"],
    ["statutory","ˈstætʃətri","adj.","法定的","It's a [statutory] requirement to notify the local authority.","S3E3 · Jobbing","通知地方当局是一项法定要求。","ˈstætʃətɔːri"],
    ["sterile","ˈsteraɪl","adj.","无菌的","What we've done is, we've taken the jars out of the oven and they're nice and [sterile] now.","S2E2 · Cowering","我们做的是把罐子从烤箱里拿出来，现在它们很干净、无菌了。","ˈsterəl"],
    ["straightforward","ˌstreɪtˈfɔːwəd","adj.","简单的；直接的","Pleasantries over, it was time to choose what to buy, which I assumed would be fairly [straightforward].","S2E1 · Surviving","寒暄完毕，该挑买什么了，我以为这会相当简单。","ˌstreɪtˈfɔːrwərd"],
    ["subsequent","ˈsʌbsɪkwənt","adj.","随后的","Sadly, though, on [subsequent] visits over the coming days, I kept finding evidence to the contrary.","S4E4 · Cottaging","可惜，在接下来几天的后续查看中，我不断发现相反的证据。","ˈsʌbsɪkwənt"],
    ["sufficient","səˈfɪʃnt","adj.","足够的","They said we could have one lavatory, that was [sufficient].","S3E4 · Harrowing","他们说我们可以有一个厕所，那就足够了。","səˈfɪʃ(ə)nt"],
    ["susceptible","səˈseptəbl","adj.","易受影响的","OK, well if your friend's done it, he's [susceptible] to risk 12 months in prison.","S2E4 · Badgering","好，如果你朋友这么做了，他就可能面临坐牢12个月的风险。","səˈseptəb(ə)l"],
    ["symptom","ˈsɪmptəm","n.","症状","I thought, no pubs and no Manchester United, he might be having withdrawal [symptoms].","S1E5 · Pan (dem) icking","我想，没有酒吧，也没有曼联，他可能会出现戒断症状。","ˈsɪmptəm"],
    ["threshold","ˈθreʃhəʊld","n.","门槛；临界值","Their six hundred cows alone take them over the [threshold].","S5E1 · Operating","光是他们那六百头牛就超过了这个门槛。","ˈθreʃhoʊld"],
    ["tranquillity","træŋˈkwɪləti","n.","宁静","Turning countryside into a car park and introducing additional congestion visually and on the transport network harms the AONB and its [tranquillity].","S2E5 · Council-ing","把乡村变成停车场，在视觉上和交通网络上增加拥堵，会损害这片杰出自然风景区及其宁静。","træŋˈkwɪləti"],
    ["traumatic","trɔːˈmætɪk","adj.","造成心理创伤的","The piglet deaths had been too [traumatic].","S3E5 · Healing","小猪的死实在太让人难受了。","trəˈmætɪk"],
    ["trivial","ˈtrɪviəl","adj.","微不足道的","I was hoping the problem was something [trivial]","S4E8 · Landlording","我本来希望问题不大","ˈtrɪviəl"],
    ["unanimous","juˈnænɪməs","adj.","一致同意的","As the beer had had a [unanimous] thumbs up, I moved onto restaurant project number two: the potatoes.","S2E4 · Badgering","啤酒获得一致好评之后，我转向餐厅的第二个项目：土豆。","juˈnænɪməs"],
    ["unreliable","ˌʌnrɪˈlaɪəbl","adj.","不可靠的","The Lamborghini's been a bit [unreliable] since you went.","S4E3 · Crawling","你走之后，那台兰博基尼就有点靠不住了。","ˌʌnrɪˈlaɪəb(ə)l"],
    ["worthwhile","ˌwɜːθˈwaɪl","adj.","值得的","But I assured him it would all be [worthwhile].","S2E7 · Scheming","但我向他保证，这一切都会是值得的。","ˌwɜːrθˈwaɪl"]
